{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Lord of Langurs: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja57'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 57 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Āsīsavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Hope </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>7. Vānarindajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Lord of Langurs: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yassete caturo dhammā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Whoever possesses these four qualities </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vānarinda yathā tava; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like you, lord of langurs—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saccaṁ dhammo dhiti cāgo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>truth, principle, steadfastness, and generosity—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>diṭṭhaṁ so ativattatī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>escapes the visible foe. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Vānarindajātakaṁ sattamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
